window.CLF_MD = {"m01-02-what-is-cloud-computing.md":"# Module 1: Introduction to the Cloud › What is Cloud Computing?\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m01-02-what-is-cloud-computing-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nYou work for a local charity organization. Your organization has sensitive data that must remain within your country for compliance reasons. However, you also need a solution that can scale quickly to handle seasonal spikes in demand. You decide to keep on-premises resources for compliance and use cloud-based resources for dynamic scaling. Which type of cloud deployment does this situation describe?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. On-premises deployment\n- [ ] B. Public cloud deployment\n- [x] C. Hybrid deployment\n- [ ] D. Data-compliance deployment\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: With a hybrid cloud solution, you can keep sensitive data on-premises to meet compliance requirements while using cloud-based resources for dynamic scaling.\n","m01-03-benefits-of-the-aws-cloud.md":"# Module 1: Introduction to the Cloud › Benefits of the AWS Cloud\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m01-03-benefits-of-the-aws-cloud-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA retail business plans to launch a new line of clothing, but they are struggling with accurately predicting how much server capacity they will need to support the launch.Which benefit of the AWS Cloud is most relevant to this situation?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Stop spending money to run and maintain data centers.\n- [x] B. Stop guessing capacity.\n- [ ] C. Trade upfront expense for variable expense.\n- [ ] D. Go global in minutes.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: With the AWS Cloud, the company can conveniently scale resources up or down based on actual demand, eliminating the need to guess future capacity requirements.\n","m01-04-introduction-to-aws-global-infrastructure.md":"# Module 1: Introduction to the Cloud › Introduction to AWS Global Infrastructure\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m01-04-introduction-to-aws-global-infrastructure-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nYou just joined a tech start-up, and the business is growing rapidly. Your new company decides that they need to design a resilient and scalable infrastructure on AWS to handle increased traffic and help ensure high availability.Which statement BEST describes the AWS Global Infrastructure benefit of high availability?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS has many customer support options to make sure the answers to your questions are highly available on its website.\n- [x] B. AWS provides multiple data centers across different geographic regions so your website can remain operational even if one location faces issues.\n- [ ] C. AWS offers a single, highly secure data center that can handle all your traffic, which makes sure that your website is available.\n- [ ] D. AWS stores all of your website’s data in a single AWS storage bucket to centralize data management.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS does provide multiple data centers across different geographic regions. This setup enhances high availability by making sure that your online store can handle increased traffic even during unforeseen events.\n","m01-05-the-aws-shared-responsibility-model.md":"# Module 1: Introduction to the Cloud › The AWS Shared Responsibility Model\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m01-05-the-aws-shared-responsibility-model-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nYou work for a startup company that is developing an application in the cloud. A new security update is available for your operating system (OS), and you are tasked with verifying that the OS is patched accordingly. Which statement BEST describes which party is responsible for applying security patches to the OS that is running in the cloud?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. The OS vendor applies the patches.\n- [ ] B. AWS is responsible for applying security patches to the OS.\n- [x] C. Your company is responsible applying security patches to the OS.\n- [ ] D. Both AWS and the customer apply separate patches.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The customer is responsible for managing the security configurations and patches for the OS running in the cloud.\n","m01-07-assessment.md":"# Module 1: Introduction to the Cloud › Assessment\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m01-07-assessment-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nYou are a software developer working for a company that is planning to migrate its existing application to the cloud. Your team lead has asked you to explain the client-server model to the rest of the team and how cloud computing fits into this model. Which statement BEST describes the client-server model and its relationship to cloud computing?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. In the client-server model, the client sends requests to the server, which processes the requests and sends back responses. Cloud computing provides scalable server resources that can be accessed over the internet.\n- [ ] B. In the client-server model, the server only handles data storage, and the client performs all processing tasks. Cloud computing provides data storage, but not processing power.\n- [ ] C. The client-server model is outdated and no longer used in modern applications. Cloud computing has replaced it completely.\n- [ ] D. In the client-server model, the client is responsible for securing their data, and the server is responsible for securing the physical hardware. Cloud computing replaces the client-server model.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: This answer accurately describes the client-server model where the client sends requests to the server. The server processes these requests and returns the appropriate responses. Cloud computing provides scalable and flexible server resources that can be accessed over the internet.\n\n<!-- id: m01-07-assessment-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nA small business is considering migrating their IT infrastructure to the cloud. The finance team has a meeting with the IT department to discuss the costs associated with this transition. During the meeting, the finance manager says they like the idea of the reliability that comes with the cloud, but they are worried about the fixed costs. Which statement accurately defines the cloud computing model and addresses the finance manager's concern?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Cloud computing involves purchasing dedicated servers and setting up a private data center. This model often comes with fixed costs related to hardware and maintenance.\n- [ ] B. Cloud computing is basically just using someone else's server to host your website, and it does not offer any sort of significant cost advantages over traditional hosting solutions.\n- [ ] C. Cloud computing reduces the need for additional hardware but still involves significant fixed monthly fees.\n- [x] D. Cloud computing is a model for delivering IT resources over the internet. Businesses can rent services on a pay-as-you-go basis, which can help reduce fixed costs and allow for more flexible budgeting.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Cloud computing can be defined as the on-demand delivery of IT resources over the internet with pay-as-you-go pricing. This answer accurately defines cloud computing and directly addresses the finance manager’s concern about fixed costs.\n\n<!-- id: m01-07-assessment-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nA government agency wants to maintain complete control over its IT infrastructure, but plans to use AWS Cloud services for specific applications. Which deployment type is BEST for this situation?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Cloud\n- [ ] B. Compliance\n- [x] C. Hybrid\n- [ ] D. On-premises\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Hybrid deployment is a solution where the agency can maintain control over on-premises systems while using cloud services for other applications.\n\n<!-- id: m01-07-assessment-q4 -->\n## Question 4\n\nA large enterprise is looking to lower operational costs. They are hoping to reduce the operational overhead associated with managing their own physical infrastructure. Which choice BEST describes which advantage of the cloud this enterprise can benefit from?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Increase speed and agility\n- [x] B. Stop spending money running and maintaining data centers\n- [ ] C. Benefit from massive economies of scale\n- [ ] D. Stop guessing capacity\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: By moving to the cloud, the enterprise can offload the responsibility of maintaining physical data centers, reducing operational overhead.\n\n<!-- id: m01-07-assessment-q5 -->\n## Question 5\n\nYou work for a sports apparel company that is expanding its operations to global customers. The company wants to deploy resources to multiple AWS locations to achieve high availability. You are tasked with explaining the basics of AWS Global Infrastructure to your chief operating officer (COO). The COO needs help understanding the difference between AWS Regions and Availability Zones. Which statement BEST describes the difference between AWS Regions and Availability Zones?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. A Region is a single data center, and an Availability Zone consists of multiple data centers.\n- [ ] B. An Availability Zone spans multiple physical locations across Regions, and Regions are located across the world.\n- [x] C. A Region is a geographical location that contains three or more Availability Zones. An Availability Zone is a distinct location within a Region that contains one or more discrete data centers.\n- [ ] D. An Availability Zone is a geographical location that contains three or more Regions. A Region is a distinct location within an Availability Zone that contains one or more discrete data centers.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: A Region is a physical location around the world that contains multiple, isolated data centers. An Availability Zone consists of one or more discrete data centers, each with independent power, networking, and connectivity.\n\n<!-- id: m01-07-assessment-q6 -->\n## Question 6\n\nYour company is planning to launch a new web application that will serve users around the world. To help ensure the application performs well and remains reliable, the IT team plans to use AWS for its vast global infrastructure. What BEST describes the benefits of AWS Global Infrastructure related to this situation? (Select TWO.)\n\n_Choose 2_\n\n- [x] A. High availability\n- [ ] B. Ease of use\n- [ ] C. Cost savings\n- [x] D. Fault tolerance\n- [ ] E. Compliance with regulatory standards\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Global infrastructure typically involves distributing resources across multiple data centers in different geographic locations. By having redundant systems in various locations, global infrastructure enhances fault tolerance. If one component fails, others can take over to minimize downtime and help ensure high availability.Ease of use, compliance, and cost savings are benefits that can be achieved by using cloud resources. However, in this case, the focus is on making resources highly available to global users.\n\n<!-- id: m01-07-assessment-q7 -->\n## Question 7\n\nA finance company is interested in migrating to the cloud. They are curious if they will have enough staff to secure both their office space and the physical infrastructure of their cloud computing resources.Which statement BEST describes the company's responsibility when it comes to securing physical infrastructure of the cloud?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. AWS is responsible for securing the physical infrastructure, and the company can focus on securing their data and applications within the cloud.\n- [ ] B. The company does not have any responsibility when it comes to security in the cloud.\n- [ ] C. The company shares responsibility with the cloud provider for securing the physical infrastructure.\n- [ ] D. The company is fully responsible for securing all physical infrastructure of the cloud, including data centers.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS is responsible for the physical security of data centers. This includes measures like access controls, surveillance, and environmental controls. Companies migrating to the cloud still have responsibilities such as security configurations and data within their cloud environments.\n\n<!-- id: m01-07-assessment-q8 -->\n## Question 8\n\nYou are a cloud architect at a company that has recently migrated its infrastructure to AWS. Your manager has asked you to debrief your team on which responsibilities the customer has when it comes to securing cloud resources. What is the customer's responsibility, based on the AWS Shared Responsibility Model? (Select TWO.)\n\n_Choose 2_\n\n- [ ] A. Physical security of data centers\n- [x] B. Managing operating system (OS) patches\n- [x] C. Encrypting client-side data\n- [ ] D. Networking and infrastructure hardware maintenance\n- [ ] E. Updating compute, networking, storage, and database software\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: In the AWS Shared Responsibility Model, the customer is responsible for managing OS patches. AWS provides the underlying infrastructure, but the customer must make sure that their OSs are up to date with the latest security patches. The customer is also responsible for encrypting client-side data. AWS provides various services to help with encryption, but it is the customer’s responsibility to implement and manage these services.Physical security of data centers and hardware maintenance are AWS responsibilities. Updating software for compute, networking, storage, and database services is also an AWS responsibility.\n","m02-01-introduction-to-amazon-ec2.md":"# Module 2: Compute in the Cloud › Introduction to Amazon EC2\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m02-01-introduction-to-amazon-ec2-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nHow does Amazon EC2 compare to running servers on premises?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. It is more expensive but offers more control.\n- [ ] B. It requires more time to set up and maintain.\n- [ ] C. It is only useful for large businesses.\n- [x] D. It is more flexible, cost-effective, and quicker to get started.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon EC2 is designed to be flexible, cost-effective, and quick to set up compared to on-premises servers.\n\n<!-- id: m02-01-introduction-to-amazon-ec2-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nWhat is multi-tenancy in the context of Amazon EC2 instances?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Each virtual machine is isolated but shares resources from a host machine.\n- [ ] B. A server can only run one type of application.\n- [ ] C. Only one user can use the instance at a time.\n- [ ] D. Multiple servers run in the same data center.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Multi-tenancy allows multiple virtual machines to share resources on the same physical host, with isolation between them.\n\n<!-- id: m02-01-introduction-to-amazon-ec2-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nA company uses Amazon EC2 instances to deploy their application. What would happen if they need to stop or terminate the EC2 instances?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Your instances are permanently deleted and cannot be recovered.\n- [ ] B. You are still charged for the instances.\n- [ ] C. The instances will automatically restart after a set time.\n- [x] D. You pay only for running instances, not for stopped or terminated ones.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: With Amazon EC2, you only pay for running instances, not for ones that are stopped or terminated.\n\n<!-- id: m02-01-introduction-to-amazon-ec2-q4 -->\n## Question 4\n\nWhat must be specified when preparing to launch an Amazon EC2 instance?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. The amount of storage and the number of users\n- [x] B. The type of instance and the operating system\n- [ ] C. The network bandwidth and data transfer limit\n- [ ] D. The instance's location and backup plan\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: You need to the choose EC2 instance type (how powerful you want it) and the Amazon Machine Image (AMI), which determines the operating system and software for your instance.\n","m02-02-amazon-ec2-instance-types.md":"# Module 2: Compute in the Cloud › Amazon EC2 Instance Types\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m02-02-amazon-ec2-instance-types-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA financial institution is running a real-time analytics application that processes large datasets stored across multiple servers to provide quick query results. The application requires fast processing of data with a focus on handling large volumes of information efficiently.Which Amazon EC2 instance type would be the BEST choice for this task?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. General purpose\n- [ ] B. Compute optimized\n- [ ] C. Storage optimized\n- [x] D. Memory optimized\n\n<!-- id: m02-02-amazon-ec2-instance-types-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nA retail company is setting up a solution to analyze historical sales data that is stored locally. The solution requires fast access to large datasets with consistent, high disk throughput for quick data retrieval.Which Amazon EC2 instance type would be the MOST suitable for this use case?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Compute optimized\n- [x] B. Storage optimized\n- [ ] C. General purpose\n- [ ] D. Accelerated computing\n","m02-03-how-to-provision-aws-resources.md":"# Module 2: Compute in the Cloud › How to Provision AWS Resources\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m02-03-how-to-provision-aws-resources-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nWhat is a primary advantage of using the AWS Command Line Interface (AWS CLI) over the AWS Management Console?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. It provides a visual, drag-and-drop interface for managing AWS resources.\n- [ ] B. It is only available for Windows users.\n- [ ] C. It requires fewer configurations and is ideal for one-time manual provisioning.\n- [x] D. It uses automation and scripting, which reduces manual steps and errors.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The AWS CLI enables automation through scripting, which is more efficient and reduces manual errors compared to the console.\n\n<!-- id: m02-03-how-to-provision-aws-resources-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nWhat is the customer's responsibility when using compute services like Amazon EC2 according to the AWS shared responsibility model?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS is responsible for managing the operating system, networking, and applications on the customer's EC2 instances.\n- [ ] B. The customer is responsible for securing the physical hardware of their EC2 instances.\n- [ ] C. AWS manages the security of the cloud, and the customer manages the security of the infrastructure.\n- [x] D. The customer is responsible for configuring, securing, and managing the operating system, networking, and applications on their EC2 instances.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The customer handles the operating system, networking, and applications on the EC2 instances. AWS manages the hardware.\n","m02-04-demo-launching-an-amazon-ec2-instance.md":"# Module 2: Compute in the Cloud › Demo: Launching an Amazon EC2 Instance\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m02-04-demo-launching-an-amazon-ec2-instance-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nWhat are the required configurations when launching an Amazon EC2 instance for a web server? (Select THREE.)\n\n_Choose 3_\n\n- [x] A. Amazon Machine Image (AMI)\n- [ ] B. Load balancing\n- [x] C. Instance type\n- [ ] D. Permissions\n- [x] E. Storage\n- [ ] F. Instance termination behavior\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: To launch an EC2 instance for a web server, configure the AMI to define the operating system and software; select the instance type to allocate CPU, memory, and storage; and set up storage options, including the type and size of the volume.Load balancing, permissions, and instance termination behavior are not required when launching a basic Amazon EC2 web server.\n\n<!-- id: m02-04-demo-launching-an-amazon-ec2-instance-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nWhat is an Amazon Machine Image (AMI) used for when launching an Amazon EC2 instance?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. To choose the instance size\n- [x] B. To pre-configure the operating system and software\n- [ ] C. To store instance data\n- [ ] D. To configure networking settings\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: An AMI is a pre-configured virtual machine image that contains the operating system, application server, and applications. This helps to launch EC2 instances quickly with the desired software and settings.\n","m02-05-amazon-ec2-pricing.md":"# Module 2: Compute in the Cloud › Amazon EC2 Pricing\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m02-05-amazon-ec2-pricing-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA financial services company needs to run sensitive applications that handle confidential customer data and require compliance with industry regulations. They need complete control over the physical server, including instance placement and resource allocation.Which pricing option should they choose?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Savings Plans\n- [ ] B. Spot Instances\n- [ ] C. On Demand\n- [x] D. Dedicated Hosts\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Dedicated Hosts provide exclusive use of a physical server, providing full control over placement and resource allocation. This is ideal for security-sensitive and licensing-specific workloads.\n\n<!-- id: m02-05-amazon-ec2-pricing-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nA startup is running a batch processing workload that can tolerate occasional interruptions, and they want to reduce costs by taking advantage of unused Amazon EC2 capacity.Which pricing option would offer them the most savings?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Reserved Instances\n- [ ] B. On Demand\n- [x] C. Spot Instances\n- [ ] D. Savings Plans\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Spot Instances offer up to 90 percent off On-Demand pricing, making them the most cost-effective option for workloads that can tolerate interruptions.\n\n<!-- id: m02-05-amazon-ec2-pricing-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nA customer is building a new application and is unsure of their usage patterns but expects to grow and stabilize usage over time. They want to start without a long-term commitment.Which pricing option should they use?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Savings Plans\n- [ ] B. Spot Instances\n- [ ] C. Reserved Instances\n- [x] D. On Demand\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: On-Demand pricing is ideal for starting without commitment. The customer can test and adjust based on actual usage before committing to longer-term options.\n","m02-06-scaling-amazon-ec2.md":"# Module 2: Compute in the Cloud › Scaling Amazon EC2\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m02-06-scaling-amazon-ec2-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nWhat is the primary benefit of scalability and elasticity in AWS?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. The ability to permanently increase resource capacity for long-term growth\n- [ ] B. The ability to manually adjust resources based on peak usage\n- [x] C. The ability to grow and shrink resources dynamically based on real-time demand\n- [ ] D. The ability to create fixed resources that never change in size\n\n> Correct! Rationale: By using scalability and elasticity, businesses can adjust resources as needed for optimal performance and cost-efficiency.\n\n<!-- id: m02-06-scaling-amazon-ec2-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nWhat is the main reason for deploying Amazon EC2 instances across multiple Availability Zones?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. To provide high availability by allowing instances in different Availability Zones to handle traffic if one Availability Zone fails\n- [ ] B. To automatically scale instances based on resource usage in each Availability Zone\n- [ ] C. To increase the power and speed of each individual instance\n- [ ] D. To decrease the cost of instances by distributing them evenly across AWS Regions\n\n> Correct! Rationale: By deploying instances across multiple Availability Zones, businesses can avoid service disruption in the event of an Availability Zone failure.\n\n<!-- id: m02-06-scaling-amazon-ec2-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nHow does AWS make sure that a business can meet fluctuating demand without over-provisioning resources?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. By providing fixed resources that are always available\n- [ ] B. By offering resources that are always running, regardless of demand\n- [ ] C. By requiring businesses to purchase excess resources in advance to handle peak demand\n- [x] D. By allowing businesses to provision resources that automatically scale based on demand\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The AWS scalability and elasticity features automatically adjust resources to meet demand, resulting cost-efficiency and performance.\n","m02-07-directing-traffic-with-elastic-load-balancing.md":"# Module 2: Compute in the Cloud › Directing Traffic with Elastic Load Balancing\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m02-07-directing-traffic-with-elastic-load-balancing-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nHow does Elastic Load Balancing (ELB) improve scalability in AWS?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. It manually adjusts the number of Amazon EC2 instances based on traffic.\n- [x] B. It automatically routes traffic to instances based on various routing methods.\n- [ ] C. It directly increases the size of Amazon EC2 instances.\n- [ ] D. It creates new Amazon EC2 instances for each request.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: ELB improves scalability by automatically distributing traffic to the EC2 instances with the least load, resulting in efficient traffic management. ELB scales elastically. This means it adjusts traffic routing based on demand without increasing hourly costs, which is a key benefit.\n\n<!-- id: m02-07-directing-traffic-with-elastic-load-balancing-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nWhich task does Elastic Load Balancing (ELB) perform?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Distributes a workload across several Amazon EC2 instances.\n- [ ] B. Removes unneeded Amazon EC2 instances when demand is low.\n- [ ] C. Adds a second Amazon EC2 instance during an online store's popular sale.\n- [ ] D. Automatically adjusts the number of Amazon EC2 instances to match demand.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: ELB and Auto Scaling work together to efficiently manage varying levels of demand. ELB is responsible for distributing incoming traffic evenly across multiple EC2 instances. This makes sure that no single instance becomes overwhelmed. It also serves as a single-entry point for traffic into an Auto Scaling group, directing requests to the appropriate resources.Meanwhile, Auto Scaling automatically adjusts the number of EC2 instances based on the demand. It adds or removes instances as needed for optimal performance and resource usage. Together, ELB and Auto Scaling help maintain application reliability and cost efficiency.\n","m02-08-messaging-and-queuing.md":"# Module 2: Compute in the Cloud › Messaging and Queuing\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m02-08-messaging-and-queuing-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nWhat BEST describes the key difference between tightly coupled and loosely coupled architectures?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. In a tightly coupled architecture, components are tightly connected and dependent on each other, whereas in a loosely coupled architecture, components can operate independently.\n- [ ] B. Tightly coupled architectures are designed for scalability, whereas loosely coupled systems focus on maintaining high availability.\n- [ ] C. Loosely coupled systems require components to share data directly with each other, whereas tightly coupled systems store data in a central repository.\n- [ ] D. Tightly coupled systems are more flexible in adding new components, whereas loosely coupled systems require careful configuration to add new components.\n\n> Correct! Rationale: In tightly coupled systems, components are heavily interdependent. If one component fails, it can cause cascading failures. In contrast, loosely coupled systems have components that operate independently, so the failure of one component does not disrupt the entire system.\n\n<!-- id: m02-08-messaging-and-queuing-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nIn a banking system, when customers transfer money, the transaction details are sent from the transaction service to a fraud detection service for verification. Sometimes, the fraud detection service is temporarily down.What is the MAIN advantage of using Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) in this banking scenario?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. It speeds up transaction processing by avoiding the use of a buffer.\n- [x] B. It stores transaction details until the fraud detection service can process them, even if the service is down.\n- [ ] C. It guarantees immediate approval of transactions.\n- [ ] D. It forces the transaction service and fraud detection service to depend on each other directly.\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon SQS safely stores transaction details until the fraud detection service can process them, preventing data loss when the service is unavailable.\n","m02-09-assessment.md":"# Module 2: Compute in the Cloud › Assessment\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nWhich option BEST describes how compute resources are provisioned and managed in the cloud?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Resources are provisioned based on demand, allowing for scaling and management.\n- [ ] B. Compute resources are fixed and cannot be scaled.\n- [ ] C. Compute resources require constant manual management.\n- [ ] D. Resources must be pre-purchased and installed onsite.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Cloud computing resources are dynamic and can be adjusted in real-time to meet changing demand, allowing for easier scaling and management.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nA media company is working on a project that involves rendering complex visual effects and simulations. The rendering process requires significant computational power and hardware accelerators to handle the intense workload efficiently.Which Amazon EC2 instance type would be the BEST choice for this task?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Compute optimized\n- [ ] B. General purpose\n- [x] C. Accelerated computing\n- [ ] D. Memory optimized\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Accelerated computing instances are equipped with GPUs and hardware accelerators, making them ideal for rendering tasks that require high computational power and efficiency.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nA startup company is building a new web application and chooses general purpose Amazon EC2 instances to host the application.Why did they choose this instance type?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. It provides the highest performance for compute-heavy tasks, such as video rendering or machine learning.\n- [ ] B. It is designed for high storage capacity, which is needed to host large databases.\n- [x] C. It provides a balanced mix of compute, memory, and networking resources while keeping costs efficient as they scale their user base.\n- [ ] D. It is specifically designed for memory-intensive applications, which is ideal for hosting a web application.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: General purpose instances offer a good balance of resources for various types of workloads, including web applications, making them a flexible and cost-effective choice.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q4 -->\n## Question 4\n\nA university research team is running climate modeling simulations that require substantial CPU power to process complex algorithms and analyze large datasets.Why are compute optimized Amazon EC2 instances ideal for this task?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. They are ideal for tasks that require significant CPU power to perform computations.\n- [ ] B. They are designed for workloads that require a high amount of memory to process large datasets efficiently.\n- [ ] C. They are optimized for handling tasks that require hardware accelerators.\n- [ ] D. They provide high storage throughput, making them ideal for tasks that require fast data retrieval and storage for large datasets.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Compute optimized instances are specifically designed for compute-heavy workloads like simulations, offering higher CPU performance to process complex algorithms and analyze large datasets.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q5 -->\n## Question 5\n\nWhat does multi-tenancy refer to in the context of Amazon EC2?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. EC2 instances dedicated to individual clients\n- [ ] B. Instances that are restricted to one geographical region\n- [x] C. Multiple users sharing the same EC2 instance while maintaining isolation\n- [ ] D. Each EC2 instance running in its own private network\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Multi-tenancy in Amazon EC2 refers to multiple tenants, or users, sharing the same instance but maintaining isolation for security and performance.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q6 -->\n## Question 6\n\nWhich tool can be used to interact with AWS services through a graphical user interface (GUI)?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Software Development Kit (AWS SDK)\n- [ ] B. Amazon EC2\n- [x] C. AWS Management Console\n- [ ] D. AWS Command Line Interface (AWS CLI)\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The AWS Management Console is the web-based GUI that is used to interact with AWS services.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q7 -->\n## Question 7\n\nA company has critical steady-state workloads and batch jobs that are not time-sensitive.How should they optimize costs using Amazon EC2 Savings Plans and Spot Instances?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Use Savings Plans for critical workloads and Spot Instances for jobs that are not time-sensitive to maximize savings.\n- [ ] B. Use Savings Plans for non-time-sensitive workloads and Spot Instances for critical jobs.\n- [ ] C. Use Spot Instances for all workloads to maximize savings and avoid Savings Plans.\n- [ ] D. Use Savings Plans for all workloads and avoid Spot Instances because of interruption risks.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: This is the best approach. Savings Plans are ideal for critical workloads that need consistent capacity and predictable pricing. Spot Instances offer significant savings for jobs that are not time-sensitive and can tolerate interruptions.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q8 -->\n## Question 8\n\nA marketing agency is developing a new web application and expects steady growth, but is unsure of traffic in the early months. They want flexibility without a long-term commitment.Which pricing option should they use?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Savings Plans\n- [ ] B. Reserved Instances\n- [ ] C. Spot Instances\n- [x] D. On-Demand\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: On-Demand pricing is ideal for starting without commitment. The customer can test and adjust based on actual usage before committing to longer-term options.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q9 -->\n## Question 9\n\nA manufacturing company is running a set of predictable workloads for the next 3 years and wants to optimize costs.Which option should they choose?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. On-Demand\n- [ ] B. Spot Instances\n- [ ] C. Dedicated Hosts\n- [x] D. Reserved Instances\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Reserved Instances offer up to a 75 percent discount for steady-state, predictable workloads when committing to a 1-year or 3-year term, making them the most cost-effective option.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q10 -->\n## Question 10\n\nWhat is the primary role of an Amazon Machine Image (AMI) when scaling applications?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. It stores backup copies of application data.\n- [ ] B. It configures scaling policies for applications.\n- [ ] C. It automatically manages network traffic.\n- [x] D. It provides a consistent image to launch new instances.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AMIs launch new Amazon EC2 instances with the same software configuration and settings, providing consistency.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q11 -->\n## Question 11\n\nHow does Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling work in AWS?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling adjusts the instance type but does not change the number of instances.\n- [ ] B. Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling requires manual intervention to add or remove instances based on traffic.\n- [ ] C. Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling adds instances when the workload is too high, but it does not scale down when demand decreases.\n- [x] D. Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling automatically adds or removes instances based on performance data and application metrics.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: For optimal resource usage, Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling automatically adjusts the number of instances based on performance metrics.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q12 -->\n## Question 12\n\nHow do Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling and Elastic Load Balancing (ELB) work together in AWS?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. They operate independently and are not connected.\n- [ ] B. Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling handles traffic routing, whereas ELB manages instance scaling.\n- [ ] C. ELB automatically scales the EC2 instances, and Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling adjusts traffic.\n- [x] D. Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling adjusts the number of instances, whereas ELB distributes traffic evenly across them.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling automatically adjusts the number of EC2 instances in response to changes in demand. ELB distributes incoming traffic evenly across those instances, supporting high availability and reliability.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q13 -->\n## Question 13\n\nWhat happens if one component fails in a loosely coupled architecture?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. The system automatically switches to backup components without any intervention.\n- [x] B. The system can continue to function as other components are independent.\n- [ ] C. The failure causes the entire system to fail.\n- [ ] D. Other components must be manually restarted.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Loosely coupled systems are designed so that components are independent. If one component fails, the rest of the system can continue to function normally, minimizing the impact of the failure.\n\n<!-- id: m02-09-assessment-q14 -->\n## Question 14\n\nA software development company needs to notify the engineering team whenever a new bug is reported in their bug tracking system. Some team members need to be notified immediately, whereas others can process the bug reports later.Which service should the software development company choose based on the requirements?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS)\n- [x] B. Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS)\n- [ ] C. Elastic Load Balancing (ELB)\n- [ ] D. Amazon EC2\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon SNS is the better choice because it delivers notifications in real time to multiple recipients simultaneously. This suits the need for immediate notifications to engineers about new bugs.\n","m03-02-aws-lambda.md":"# Module 3: Exploring Compute Services › AWS Lambda\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m03-02-aws-lambda-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA development team at a fintech startup is building a new customer-facing microservice using AWS Lambda. AWS takes care of the infrastructure, but the team is focused on meeting strict security and compliance requirements. Which task is still the team's responsibility when using Lambda?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Scaling the infrastructure\n- [ ] B. Patching the underlying operating system\n- [ ] C. Managing server availability\n- [x] D. Managing data access permissions\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Although AWS manages the infrastructure, the team is responsible for correctly configuring AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) roles and permissions for any services that the Lambda function accesses.\n\n<!-- id: m03-02-aws-lambda-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nA photography company offers cloud-based photo editing and storage. To streamline operations, it uses AWS Lambda to automatically process photos—resizing images, applying filters, and organizing files—every time a client uploads a new image. Which key components are involved in running an automated photo processing workflow with Lambda?\n\n_Choose 3_\n\n- [x] A. Lambda function\n- [x] B. Triggers\n- [ ] C. Server provisioning\n- [x] D. Runtimes\n- [ ] E. Manual scaling configuration\n- [ ] F. Operating system selection\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The key components of AWS Lambda are the function, triggers, and runtimes. These components handle code, respond to events, and provide the language environment. Customers do not need to manage servers, scaling, or operating systems. AWS takes care of all that.\n","m03-03-containers-and-orchestration-on-aws.md":"# Module 3: Exploring Compute Services › Containers and Orchestration on AWS\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m03-03-containers-and-orchestration-on-aws-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA developer just finished building an application that runs flawlessly on their laptop. However, when their team tries to deploy it in a different environment, it crashes because of missing dependencies and configuration mismatches. How do containers help solve this problem?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. By providing access to multiple operating systems for compatibility testing\n- [ ] B. By automatically scaling the application across multiple cloud providers\n- [x] C. By packaging the application and everything it needs to run into one consistent environment\n- [ ] D. By eliminating the need to write configuration files\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Containers bundle the application with all of its dependencies and configuration, so it runs the same across different environments.\n","m03-04-additional-compute-services.md":"# Module 3: Exploring Compute Services › Additional Compute Services\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m03-04-additional-compute-services-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA startup is building a web application and wants a simple way to deploy code without managing infrastructure. They need to have auto scaling and monitoring handled for them. Which AWS service should they use?\n\n_Choose 2_\n\n- [x] A. AWS Elastic Beanstalk\n- [ ] B. Amazon EC2\n- [x] C. AWS Batch\n- [ ] D. AWS Outposts\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Elastic Beanstalk handles deployment, scaling, and monitoring for web applications with minimal setup. Rationale: AWS Batch is designed for compute-heavy jobs, not web application deployment.\n\n<!-- id: m03-04-additional-compute-services-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nA financial company must run workloads on premises because of strict compliance requirements, but it wants to use AWS services and tools consistently across environments. Which service meets their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Elastic Beanstalk\n- [ ] B. AWS Batch\n- [x] C. AWS Outposts\n- [ ] D. Amazon Lightsail\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Outposts extends AWS infrastructure to on-premises environments with consistent tools and APIs.\n","m03-05-assessment.md":"# Module 3: Exploring Compute Services › Assessment\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m03-05-assessment-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nWhat is the customer responsible for managing in a serverless service like AWS Lambda?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. The physical servers and networking hardware\n- [ ] B. The operating system, network configuration, and application stack\n- [ ] C. Nothing—AWS manages everything\n- [x] D. The application code\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: With serverless services like Lambda, customers are responsible for the application code. AWS manages the infrastructure, scaling, and availability.\n\n<!-- id: m03-05-assessment-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nA developer is launching a new microservice and wants to focus only on writing and deploying code. They do not want to manage servers, handle scaling, or worry about infrastructure availability. Which AWS service model is BEST for this use case?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Unmanaged\n- [ ] B. On premises\n- [x] C. Serverless\n- [ ] D. Hybrid cloud\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: With serverless services, customers can focus solely on writing and deploying code. AWS fully manages infrastructure, scaling, and availability, so customers do not have to worry about managing servers or capacity.\n\n<!-- id: m03-05-assessment-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nWhich scenario is the BEST fit for using AWS Lambda?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Automatically processing images as users upload them to an Amazon S3 bucket\n- [ ] B. Running a relational database that needs complex queries and frequent connections\n- [ ] C. Hosting a high-traffic web server that requires full control over the operating system (OS)\n- [ ] D. Running a large, high-performance computing workload that takes several hours to complete\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Lambda is perfect for this event-driven use case. It can run code in response to uploads and scale automatically based on the number of events.\n\n<!-- id: m03-05-assessment-q4 -->\n## Question 4\n\nA company is launching a containerized photo application and has built the container image, which needs to be stored securely. They plan to use Kubernetes for orchestration and prefer not to manage any servers. Which combination of AWS services BEST fits their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon S3, Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS), and Amazon EC2\n- [x] B. Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR), Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS), and AWS Fargate\n- [ ] C. Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR), AWS Lambda, and Amazon EC2\n- [ ] D. Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR), Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS), and Amazon EC2\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon ECR stores container images, Amazon EKS handles Kubernetes orchestration, and AWS Fargate runs containers without server management. This combination offers seamless orchestration with no infrastructure maintenance.\n\n<!-- id: m03-05-assessment-q5 -->\n## Question 5\n\nA development team at a travel company has stored their hotel booking system’s container image in Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) and is ready to deploy it. They need a service that can automatically start and stop containers based on traffic, scale up or down with demand, and monitor the health of the system. Which service does the team need next?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon EC2 with auto scaling\n- [x] B. An orchestration service like Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) or Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS)\n- [ ] C. A virtual machine to run the container manually\n- [ ] D. AWS Lambda\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon ECS or Amazon EKS can automatically scale containers, handle health checks, and manage their lifecycle based on traffic demand, which fits the team’s requirements.\n\n<!-- id: m03-05-assessment-q6 -->\n## Question 6\n\nA development team at an e-commerce company is working on a new website. The application runs fine on their local machines, but when they attempt to deploy it to a staging environment, it does not work as expected. The team wants to make sure that the application runs consistently across all development, testing, and production environments going forward. Which solution should the team use to make sure that the application runs the same across all environments?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Set up separate environments for each operating system.\n- [ ] B. Use different versions of the applications for different environments.\n- [ ] C. Use Amazon EC2 to manually recreate the development environment.\n- [x] D. Package the application in a container that includes all dependencies.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Containers bundle the application, runtime, and dependencies together, providing consistency across all environments from development to production.\n\n<!-- id: m03-05-assessment-q7 -->\n## Question 7\n\nA pharmaceutical research company needs to run thousands of simulations to analyze protein folding. These compute-heavy tasks are run in parallel and do not require real-time interaction. The company wants the jobs to be automatically scheduled and scaled based on computing demand. Which AWS service BEST fits this workload?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. AWS Batch\n- [ ] B. Amazon Lightsail\n- [ ] C. AWS Elastic Beanstalk\n- [ ] D. AWS Lambda\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS Batch is designed for large-scale batch workloads and can automatically manage and scale compute resources for job queues.\n\n<!-- id: m03-05-assessment-q8 -->\n## Question 8\n\nA freelance developer is building a blog for a client with minimal traffic. They want a basic, cost-effective solution that includes storage and compute in one package, without having to deal with complex configurations or scaling concerns. Which AWS service is the BEST fit?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Fargate\n- [x] B. Amazon Lightsail\n- [ ] C. AWS Batch\n- [ ] D. AWS Lambda\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Lightsail is great for small projects like blogs and basic websites, and it offers predictable pricing and ease of use.\n","m04-04-infrastructure-and-automation.md":"# Module 4: Going Global › Infrastructure and Automation\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m04-04-infrastructure-and-automation-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA rapidly growing tech startup company is planning to launch a new web application that will require a complex infrastructure setup, including multiple Amazon EC2 instances, Elastic Load Balancing, and Auto Scaling groups. The application must be deployed consistently across different environments. Would AWS CloudFormation be a good solution for managing the company's infrastructure?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. CloudFormation should be used only for setting up static websites, not for complex applications.\n- [ ] B. CloudFormation is too complicated and would slow down the deployment process.\n- [x] C. CloudFormation would be ideal because it supports infrastructure as code (IaC), enabling consistent, repeatable deployments across different environments.\n- [ ] D. CloudFormation would not be useful in this scenario because it only supports simple infrastructure setups.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: CloudFormation is designed to handle complex infrastructure setups. It defines infrastructure as code to help make sure that deployments are consistent across different environments such as development, testing, and production.\n","m04-02-choosing-aws-regions.md":"# Module 4: Going Global › Choosing AWS Regions\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m04-02-choosing-aws-regions-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA cloud engineer for a government agency is tasked with selecting an AWS Region to deploy the agency's resources. Which factors are MOST important to consider when selecting a Region?\n\n_Choose 2_\n\n- [x] A. Any regulatory compliance standards the agency requires\n- [x] B. Proximity to users\n- [ ] C. Number of files stored\n- [ ] D. Personal preference of the chief information officer\n- [ ] E. How recently the Region was constructed\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: When working for a government agency, making sure that the selected Region complies with all relevant government regulations and policies is important. This includes data sovereignty, privacy laws, and other compliance requirements. Proximity to users or data centers is also important. Close proximity reduces latency and improves the performance of applications and services.\n","m04-05-assessment.md":"# Module 4: Going Global › Assessment\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m04-05-assessment-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA nonprofit organization is migrating all of their resources to the AWS Cloud. They are trying to decide which AWS Region to deploy their resources to.Which option lists the factors the organization needs to consider when deciding where to place their cloud resources?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Software licensing, hardware specifications, cloud skillset of staff, and customer reviews\n- [ ] B. Network speed, data encryption, user interface, and storage capacity\n- [x] C. Compliance, proximity to customers, feature availability, and pricing\n- [ ] D. Server uptime, application performance, employee satisfaction, and office location\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: When deciding where to place cloud resources, companies must consider multiple factors. Compliance refers to the Region meeting legal or regulatory requirements. Proximity to customers helps reduce latency and improve user experience. Feature availability makes sure that the required AWS services are supported in the chosen Region. Pricing varies by Region, so cost-efficiency is also a critical factor.\n\n<!-- id: m04-05-assessment-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nWhat BEST describes key benefits of using multiple AWS Regions and multiple Availability Zones?\n\n_Choose 2_\n\n- [x] A. Low latency for end users\n- [ ] B. Enhanced security protocol\n- [ ] C. Increased storage capacity\n- [x] D. High availability and fault tolerance\n- [ ] E. Faster database migration\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: By using multiple AWS Regions, a company can place their resources closer to their end users, which reduces the distance that the data must travel. This results in lower latency and a better user experience. By using multiple Availability Zones within a Region, the company enhances the fault tolerance of their applications. If one zone fails, their application can continue to operate from another zone, maintaining high availability.\n\n<!-- id: m04-05-assessment-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nWhich answer BEST describes the purpose and benefits of AWS edge locations?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Edge locations are composed of physical data centers that host the majority of AWS services and applications.\n- [ ] B. Edge locations are intended to provide redundant storage solutions for critical data.\n- [ ] C. Edge locations are used exclusively for running compute-intensive applications and databases.\n- [x] D. Edge locations cache content to deliver data with lower latency and higher transfer speeds to end users.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: This answer accurately describes the purpose and benefits of AWS edge locations. They are designed to improve the delivery of content by caching it closer to end users, thus reducing latency and increasing transfer speeds.\n\n<!-- id: m04-05-assessment-q4 -->\n## Question 4\n\nWhich answer BEST describes the relationship between AWS Regions, Availability Zones, and edge locations?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Regions are physical locations around the world where AWS has multiple Availability Zones. Each Availability Zone has one or more edge location.\n- [ ] B. AWS Regions, Availability Zones, and edge locations are all the same thing and are used interchangeably.\n- [ ] C. AWS Regions contain multiple edge locations, and each edge location can have one or more Availability Zones.\n- [x] D. AWS Regions are physical locations around the world where AWS has multiple Availability Zones. Edge locations are located outside of AWS Regions and cache frequently accessed content.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS Regions are indeed physical locations around the world where AWS has multiple isolated Availability Zones. Edge locations, on the other hand, are part of the AWS content delivery network (CDN). They are optimized for content delivery, not directly tied to Availability Zones.\n\n<!-- id: m04-05-assessment-q5 -->\n## Question 5\n\nWhich answer describes the key features and benefits of AWS CloudFormation?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. With CloudFormation, users can model and set up their AWS resources using code to automate provisioning and the management of infrastructure. This method can help to reduce errors and maintain consistency across environments.\n- [ ] B. With CloudFormation, users can cache frequently accessed content. That way, users experience lower latency when accessing cloud resources.\n- [ ] C. CloudFormation is a service that provides a visual interface for manually configuring each AWS resource one by one, without the need for any code.\n- [ ] D. CloudFormation is a cost-optimization tool that analyzes the AWS usage and recommends the best practices for reducing a company's AWS bills.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: This answer accurately describes the key features and benefits of CloudFormation. It highlights the ability to model and set up resources using code, automate provisioning, reduce errors, and help maintain environment consistency.\n\n<!-- id: m04-05-assessment-q6 -->\n## Question 6\n\nA team at a biomedical tech company is tasked with deploying a new medical application across multiple AWS Regions to help maintain high availability and fault tolerance. The application consists of several components, including a web server, a database, and a message queue. The deployment needs to be consistent and repeatable and should minimize manual errors through automation.Which approach is BEST suited for deploying this application according to the needs of automation and consistency?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Using the AWS Management Console to manually deploy each component in every Region\n- [x] B. Using an Infrastructure as Code (IaC) service such as AWS CloudFormation to deploy the application\n- [ ] C. Combining console and programmatic approaches for different tiers of the application\n- [ ] D. Writing a script to programmatically deploy the application using the cloud provider's API\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: With an IaC service like CloudFormation, the team can define their infrastructure in a declarative way. This helps to version, review, and automate the deployment process for consistency and repeatability.\n","m05-01-introduction-to-networking.md":"# Module 5: Networking › Introduction to Networking\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m05-01-introduction-to-networking-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nWhat are the uses of a subnet in an Amazon VPC?\n\n_Choose 3_\n\n- [x] A. Can be used to share public resources\n- [x] B. Can be used to organize your resources\n- [ ] C. Can be used to provide high availability because they consist of one or more discrete data centers\n- [ ] D. Can provide a centralized interface for accessing and managing various AWS resources and services\n- [x] E. Can be used to isolate resources and keep them private\n- [ ] F. Can be used as an on-demand and scalable computing capacity in the AWS Cloud\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Subnets are used to organize resources, share resources publicly, or isolate resources to keep them private.\n","m05-02-organizing-aws-cloud-resources.md":"# Module 5: Networking › Organizing AWS Cloud Resources\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m05-02-organizing-aws-cloud-resources-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA company is setting up their Amazon VPC. They need to connect their corporate data center through the internet with a secure connection. They also want to make sure the resources are isolated from the public. Which solution would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. A virtual private gateway with a VPN connection and a private subnet in the Amazon VPC\n- [ ] B. An internet gateway with an Amazon VPC and a public subnet\n- [ ] C. An internet gateway with a public subnet holding the resources in the Amazon VPC\n- [ ] D. An internet gateway with an Amazon VPC and no subnets\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: A virtual private gateway with a VPN connection would work. And using a private subnet is exactly what they need!\n","m05-03-more-ways-to-connect-to-the-aws-cloud.md":"# Module 5: Networking › More Ways to Connect to the AWS Cloud\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m05-03-more-ways-to-connect-to-the-aws-cloud-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA company is conducting a large-scale migration of their on-premises data center with their data warehouse and data backup. They need a solution that will meet the large amount of bandwidth requirements during migration. The solution will also be used for their ongoing data transfers after the move because they will retain part of their on-premises data center for a hybrid cloud solution.Which AWS solution would best meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. AWS Direct Connect link to their on-premises network and the AWS Cloud\n- [ ] B. AWS Site-to-Site VPN\n- [ ] C. AWS Client VPN\n- [ ] D. AWS Private Link to their on-premises datacenter\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Direct Connect would provide the bandwidth requirements for the migration, in addition to the ongoing data transfers in their hybrid solution.\n\n<!-- id: m05-03-more-ways-to-connect-to-the-aws-cloud-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nA company is choosing the type of gateway for their network. They need to connect their corporate data center with their private subnet in their Amazon Virtual Private Cloud. Their gateway needs to allow only protected internet traffic to enter into the Amazon VPC. It should also allow a connection between their Amazon VPC and a private network only if it is coming from an approved network.Which type of gateway would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Virtual private gateway\n- [ ] B. Amazon API Gateway\n- [ ] C. AWS Transit Gateway\n- [ ] D. Internet gateway\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: A virtual private gateway is the component that allows protected internet traffic to enter into the VPC. This is perfect because it will restrict access to only protected internet traffic.\n","m05-04-subnets-security-groups-and-network-access-control-lists.md":"# Module 5: Networking › Subnets, Security Groups, and Network Access Control Lists\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m05-04-subnets-security-groups-and-network-access-control-lists-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA retail customer is setting up their application in the AWS Cloud. The application requires a lot of control in defining traffic rules for the individual Amazon EC2 instances in their public subnet. Which solution would BEST meet the requirements for securing the resources?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Change all the subnets to private subnets to avoid accessing from the public internet.\n- [ ] B. Set up network ACLs for the EC2 instances based on the application requirements.\n- [x] C. Set up security groups for the EC2 instances based on the application requirements.\n- [ ] D. Set up a public subnet with strong passwords that meet the customer's requirements.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Security groups would allow the fine-grained control at the instance level.\n\n<!-- id: m05-04-subnets-security-groups-and-network-access-control-lists-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nWhich network component performs stateless packet filtering?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Network access control list (network ACL)\n- [ ] B. Security groups\n- [ ] C. Amazon VPC\n- [ ] D. Private subnet\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Network access control lists are stateless and don't remember the previous decisions made for incoming packets.\n","m05-06-global-networking.md":"# Module 5: Networking › Global Networking\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m05-06-global-networking-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nAn enterprise customer with a worldwide sales force is looking to deliver their large library of sales training content. They want to make sure their sales force can access the media-rich training content with low latency and reduced costs.Which AWS service would BEST fit the customer's need?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Amazon CloudFront\n- [ ] B. AWS Global Accelerator\n- [ ] C. Amazon Route 53\n- [ ] D. Amazon VPC\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: CloudFront is a service that uses the AWS global network to improve application availability, performance, and security.\n\n<!-- id: m05-06-global-networking-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nAfter years of working with different domain registration companies, a media company is looking for a solution to manage all their existing domain names. They also want to register new domain names. Ideally, they would like to manage all their domain names in a single service.Which AWS service would BEST fit the customer's need?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Amazon VPC\n- [x] B. Amazon Route 53\n- [ ] C. Amazon CloudFront\n- [ ] D. AWS Global Accelerator\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon Route 53 is a highly available and scalable cloud DNS service. It will makes it possible for the customer to manage all their domains in a single service.\n","m05-07-global-architectures.md":"# Module 5: Networking › Global Architectures\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m05-07-global-architectures-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nA healthcare company is looking to create a dedicated network connection to AWS. They would use this connection for their heavy payloads of data being sent over the internet to AWS. They also have compliance requirements due to the sensitive nature of their patient data.Which type of connection to the AWS Cloud would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. VPN connection from their corporate data center to the AWS Cloud\n- [x] B. AWS Direct Connect connection from their corporate data center to a virtual private gateway in their VPC in the AWS Cloud\n- [ ] C. Standard internet connection from the client to an internet gateway in the VPC in the AWS Cloud\n- [ ] D. VPN connection from their corporate data center to a virtual private gateway to their Amazon VPC\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS Direct Connect connection would provide both the bandwidth for the large data payloads and the security requirements needed for compliance.\n","m05-08-assessment.md":"# Module 5: Networking › Assessment\n\nZaznacz poprawne odpowiedzi: zmień `[ ]` na `[x]`.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q1 -->\n## Question 1\n\nWhat is networking in the AWS Cloud?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Interconnected devices that can exchange data and resources\n- [ ] B. Physically isolated data centers or set of data centers within an AWS Region\n- [ ] C. Logically isolated section of the AWS Cloud where you can launch AWS resources in a virtual network that you define\n- [ ] D. System that translates readable domain names to IP addresses\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: You can think of networking in the AWS Cloud as the infrastructure and services working together to host your applications, data, and any other resources you might need.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q2 -->\n## Question 2\n\nWhat is the primary function of an Availability Zone in the AWS Cloud?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. It filters inbound and outbound traffic to EC2 instances in a VPC.\n- [ ] B. It provisions a logically isolated section of the AWS Cloud where you can launch AWS resources in a virtual network that you define.\n- [ ] C. It allows you to create a subsection of a virtual private cloud (VPC) where you can isolate resources and control access.\n- [x] D. It enhances application availability and fault tolerance by allowing resources to be deployed across multiple zones.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: An Availability Zone is a physically isolated data center or set of data centers within an AWS Region. Each AZ has independent power, cooling, and networking, designed to enhance application availability and fault tolerance by allowing resources to be deployed across multiple Availability Zones within the same Region.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q3 -->\n## Question 3\n\nA company wants to establish a secure, private connection between their on-premises data center and their Amazon VPC to create a hybrid cloud architecture.Which component should they use to help ensure a secure connection?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Virtual private gateway\n- [ ] B. Internet gateway\n- [ ] C. Subnet\n- [ ] D. Route table\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: A virtual private gateway is the virtual private network (VPN) endpoint on the AWS side. It provides a way for you to establish a secure, encrypted connection between your on-premises network and your virtual private cloud (VPC).\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q4 -->\n## Question 4\n\nA customer is creating an Amazon VPC for their application. They want to create a private segment in the Amazon VPC so that resources launched can be isolated from users on the internet.Which network component would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. A private subnet\n- [ ] B. An Availability Zone instead of a subnet\n- [ ] C. A public subnet\n- [ ] D. Either a public subnet or a private subnet would work\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: A private subnet is a network segment within a Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) that does not have a direct route to the internet. This would meet their needs for the application.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q5 -->\n## Question 5\n\nA retail customer is hosting their application in an Amazon VPC and wants to configure traffic rules for the Amazon EC2 instances running in a public subnet. The application requires multiple rules to be defined at the instance level. Which solution or feature would meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Set up security groups for the Amazon EC2 instances based on the application requirements.\n- [ ] B. Set up a virtual private gateway based on the application requirements.\n- [ ] C. Set up network access control lists, (network ACLs) for the Amazon EC2 instances based on the application requirements.\n- [ ] D. Change the public subnet to a private subnet to avoid public internet access.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Security groups would allow the fine-grained control at the instance level. They can define rules in the public subnet for the individual instances.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q6 -->\n## Question 6\n\nA customer is moving their application to an Amazon VPC and wants to setup a traffic control at the subnet level. They need broad control of traffic in and out and would like to use both allow and deny type rules.Which solution or feature would meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Change the public subnet to a private subnet to avoid public internet access.\n- [ ] B. Set up a virtual private gateway based on the application requirements.\n- [ ] C. Use security groups.\n- [x] D. Use network access control lists (network ACLs).\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Network ACLs would allow the broad traffic control at the subnet level. Network ACLs also have both allow and deny type rules.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q7 -->\n## Question 7\n\nA customer is exploring solutions to establish secure, encrypted connections between their on-premises networks at their data centers and branch offices. They are looking for the MOST cost-effective way to connect their office sites to other sites and their AWS services. They are not looking to increase the amount of bandwidth.Which solution would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS PrivateLink\n- [ ] B. AWS Direct Connect\n- [x] C. AWS Site-to-Site VPN\n- [ ] D. AWS Client VPN\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: AWS Site-to-Site VPN creates a secure connection between your data center or branch offices and your AWS Cloud resources.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q8 -->\n## Question 8\n\nAn enterprise customer just merged with another company and needs a way to quickly scale and provide a way for the new worldwide sales force to access their AWS resources. They want a fully managed service with advanced authentication for their new remote workers.Which solution would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Site-to-Site VPN\n- [ ] B. AWS Direct Connect\n- [ ] C. AWS PrivateLink\n- [x] D. AWS Client VPN\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Amazon Client VPN is a networking service you can use to connect your remote workers and on-premises networks to the cloud. It provides advanced authentication, and elastic and remote access in a fully managed service.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q9 -->\n## Question 9\n\nA customer wants a way to establish a dedicated connection from their on-premises network to an Amazon VPC. They need a solution that provides a more consistent network experience with increased bandwidth.Which type of connection to the AWS Cloud would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. Internet gateway\n- [x] B. AWS Direct Connect\n- [ ] C. Amazon CloudFront\n- [ ] D. Virtual private gateway\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Direct Connect would establish a dedicated connection from an on-premises network to one or more virtual private clouds (VPCs). It can also reduce network costs, increase bandwidth throughput, and provide a more consistent network experience than internet-based connections.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q10 -->\n## Question 10\n\nWhat is the primary function of a domain name service (DNS)?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. It provisions a logically isolated section of the AWS Cloud where you can launch AWS resources in a virtual network that you define.\n- [ ] B. It filters inbound and outbound traffic to Amazon EC2 instances in a virtual private cloud (VPC).\n- [x] C. It translates human-readable domain names to machine readable IP addresses.\n- [ ] D. It allows you to create a subsection of a virtual private cloud (VPC) where you can isolate resources and control access.\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: A DNS translates the domain name into your browser and sends it to a customer DNS resolver. It then asks the company DNS server for the IP address and returns it so the user can reach the website.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q11 -->\n## Question 11\n\nA customer is creating their application resources in their virtual private cloud (VPC) subnets. They want to secure their resources in the cloud, specifically the networking traffic protection tasks.Which component is the customer responsible for, based on the shared responsibility model?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Securing network traffic with the subnets and resources with Network access control lists (network ACLs) and security groups\n- [ ] B. Securing access to the AWS data centers and facilities that run AWS Cloud services\n- [ ] C. Securing the hardware that runs the AWS Cloud services\n- [ ] D. Securing the software that runs the AWS Cloud services\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: The customer is responsible for securing the network traffic. They can do this using security groups and network ACLs.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q12 -->\n## Question 12\n\nA financial customer needs a content delivery solution to deliver required training videos and static content to their financial consultants worldwide. They want to make sure the solution provides low latency.Which AWS solution would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Global Accelerator\n- [ ] B. AWS Direct Connect\n- [ ] C. Amazon Route 53\n- [x] D. Amazon CloudFront\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: CloudFront speeds up distribution of your static and dynamic web content to your users. It securely delivers your content with low latency through a worldwide network of data centers called edge locations.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q13 -->\n## Question 13\n\nA media company needs a service to manage their domain registrations with different providers. They will also be using the service to route internet traffic to their resources hosted both in the AWS Cloud and elsewhere.Which AWS solution would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [x] A. Amazon Route 53\n- [ ] B. AWS Direct Connect\n- [ ] C. AWS Global Accelerator\n- [ ] D. Amazon CloudFront\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Route 53 is a domain name system (DNS) service that manages domain registration, DNS routing, and health checks. It provides reliable and efficient routing of users to your website or applications, whether they are hosted within AWS or elsewhere.\n\n<!-- id: m05-08-assessment-q14 -->\n## Question 14\n\nA customer is exploring edge networking services to improve application availability, performance, and security. They need a solution for traffic routing when something goes wrong in one of their application's locations. Specifically, it takes into account the endpoint health, user location, and policies.Which AWS solution would BEST meet their needs?\n\n_Choose 1_\n\n- [ ] A. AWS Direct Connect\n- [ ] B. Amazon CloudFront\n- [ ] C. Amazon Route 53\n- [x] D. AWS Global Accelerator\n\n<!-- klucz: znaczniki przy odpowiedziach -->\n\n> Correct! Rationale: Global Accelerator is a network service that is designed to improve the availability and performance of applications for global users. It does this by providing static IP addresses, directing traffic over the AWS global network, and routing to optimal endpoints based on health, user location, and policies.\n"};
